Requirements: 13   with obligations: 13

[task-01] The review already runs the project's candidate tests against each edit it
    injects, and then uses the result for nothing unless the edit was separately
    checked. Checking is off, so on a normal review the result is used for nothing at
    all, and every combination of a plausible defect and a candidate test is still put
    to a model. Those calls are almost all of what a review costs, and nearly every time
    the answer is that the test would not catch the defect.
    -> candidate-defect-test-pairs-are-modeled  [functional/explicit]
       Every combination of a plausible defect and a candidate test is still put to a
       model.
    -> review-cost-is-mostly-model-calls  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       The review's cost is dominated by the model calls made for plausible defect and
       candidate test combinations.
    -> test-would-not-catch-defect  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       A test would not catch the defect in nearly every case.

[task-02] Let the run choose which of those questions are worth asking. When at least
    one candidate test failed under an edit, that edit demonstrably changed what the
    code does, so a test that went on passing under it is not sensitive to the change
    and is not asked about. The tests that failed under the same edit are still asked
    about, because a test going red does not on its own say the named defect is what it
    caught.
    -> let-run-choose-questions  [human_review/explicit]
       Let the run choose which of those questions are worth asking.
    -> edit-changed-code-behavior  [invariant/explicit]
       An edit under which at least one candidate test failed demonstrably changed what
       the code does.
    -> passing-test-not-asked-about  [functional/explicit]
       A test that went on passing under the edit is not sensitive to the change and is
       not asked about.
    -> failed-tests-still-asked-about  [regression/explicit]
       The tests that failed under the same edit are still asked about.

[task-03] When no candidate test failed under an edit, nothing was demonstrated: an edit
    that changed nothing and an edit that changed something no test watches look alike
    from outside. Every pair for that defect is asked about, exactly as if no edit had
    been built. A defect for which no edit could be built is asked about as it is today.
    -> every-pair-asked-about  [functional/explicit]
       Every pair for that defect is asked about.
    -> as-if-no-edit-had-been-built  [invariant/explicit]
       Treat the defect as if no edit had been built when no candidate test failed under
       an edit.
    -> asked-about-as-it-is-today  [compatibility/explicit]
       A defect for which no edit could be built is asked about as it is today.

[task-04] A pair dropped this way has not been decided, and must not read as though it
    had been. It is recorded with the reason it was dropped and the injection attempt
    the decision rests on, so a reader can see it was skipped rather than answered, and
    it is not a demonstration that the test fails to catch the defect.
    -> must-not-read-as-though-it-had-been  [invariant/explicit]
       The dropped pair is recorded in a way that makes clear it was skipped rather than
       answered, and it does not read as though it had been decided.
    -> record-drop-reason-and-injection-attempt  [functional/explicit]
       Record the reason it was dropped and the injection attempt the decision rests on.

[task-05] Whether running the project's tests is worth doing is the review's own
    decision, and that decision has to account for this. Until now nothing consumed the
    run unless edits were checked, and the review declined to run on that ground.
    Choosing which questions to ask is a second thing the run earns.
    -> test-run-worth-doing-is-review-decision  [human_review/explicit]
       Whether running the project's tests is worth doing is determined by the review's
       own decision.
    -> account-for-test-run-worth  [human_review/explicit]
       The review's decision about whether running the project's tests is worth doing
       accounts for this requirement.
    -> account-for-question-selection  [human_review/explicit]
       The review's decision about which questions to ask accounts for this requirement.
    -> run-consumes-only-on-edits-checked  [invariant/explicit]
       The run is consumed only when edits are checked.
    -> review-declined-to-run-on-that-ground  [human_review/explicit]
       The review declined to run on that ground.
    -> choose-questions-as-run-earn  [functional/explicit]
       The run earns the choice of which questions to ask.

[task-06] Dropping pairs can be turned off, so a review can still be run the way it runs
    today.
    -> dropping-pairs-can-be-turned-off  [functional/explicit]
       The review supports turning off dropping pairs.
    -> preserve-current-review-run-mode  [compatibility/explicit]
       Preserve the ability to run a review the way it runs today.

[task-07] For each defect the stage was asked about, the report says how many of its
    pairs the run itself decided, how many were asked of the model, and how many were
    dropped.
    -> report-counts-self-decided-pairs  [functional/explicit]
       The report states how many of its pairs the run itself decided.
    -> asked-of-model-count-reported  [functional/explicit]
       The report states how many pairs were asked of the model for each defect the
       stage was asked about.
    -> dropped-pairs-count-reported  [functional/explicit]
       The report states how many pairs were dropped.

[constraint-01] Nothing about the edit, or about what the tests did under it, reaches
    the model.
    -> model-sees-no-edit-or-test-result  [invariant/explicit]
       Nothing about the edit or about what the tests did under it reaches the model.

[constraint-02] An edit nobody checked still settles nothing. A dropped pair reaches no
    evidence tier and yields no finding.
    -> unchecked-edit-settles-nothing  [invariant/explicit]
       An edit that was not separately checked does not settle the question of whether
       it makes the named defect true.
    -> dropped-pair-no-evidence-tier  [invariant/explicit]
       A dropped pair does not reach any evidence tier and does not yield a finding.

[exclusion-01] Checking whether an edit really makes its named defect true.
    -> no-edit-checking  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not add or perform checking whether an edit really makes its
       named defect true.

[exclusion-02] Building an edit, choosing the region it falls in, or deciding whether it
    is valid.
    -> no-edit-construction-or-validation  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not include building an edit, choosing the region it falls in, or
       deciding whether it is valid.

[exclusion-03] Which tests are candidates, and whether the project's tests can be run at
    all.
    -> exclude-test-selection-and-run-eligibility  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter which tests are candidates, and it does not alter
       whether the project's tests can be run at all.

[exclusion-04] Running the project's whole test suite.
    -> no-whole-suite-run  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not run the project's whole test suite.

